    <statement><p>Find the gradient of the function
<m>f(r,h) = 2\pi rh+\pi r^{2}</m>
at the point <m>(3,3)</m>.</p>
<p><m>\nabla f(3,3) =</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left(6\pi +6\pi \right)\boldsymbol{i}+6\pi \boldsymbol{j}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><me>f_r = 2\pi h+2\pi r \quad \mbox{and}\quad f_h = 2\pi r,</me>
we have
<me>\nabla f = \left(2\pi h+2\pi r\right)\boldsymbol{i}+2\pi r\boldsymbol{j},</me>
and thus
<me>\nabla f(3,3) = \left(6\pi +6\pi \right)\boldsymbol{i}+6\pi \boldsymbol{j}.</me>



</solution>
